      ],
      "visible": true,
      "showLabel": false,
      "data": {
        "title": "Every concept needed to explain Twilite has one canonical specification, separating meaning, representation and implementation evidence",
        "body": "Approved review decisions, 2026-09-25. The library defines the graph language; registry membership alone does not establish primitive status. Record semantic responsibility separately from its representation as a node, edge, chain, or composed graph. Surface is a named presentation track and Edge is a relationship, even though neither is a node type.\n\nEach spec has eight sections: Meaning, Invariants, Contract, Ports and Relationships, Behavior, Representations, Explicitly Not Part of This Primitive, Examples. Separate agreed semantics, implemented behavior with source/test evidence, known gaps with task references, and unresolved decisions. Structural validation is not proof of runtime or visual behavior.\n\nA Surface starts with a View representation and ends in a Glyph. A View may render glyph-shaped artwork; it does not have to be an icon View and does not replace the terminal Glyph. Surface selection, resolution and focus do not implicitly resize the workspace frame or move the camera. Manual resizing is explicit; internal rendering is clipped and exposed boundary controls remain accessible.\n\nWork order: specification form; reconcile Declaration/Surface/Bridge; Content and View together; Glyph and Surface boundary review; Port/Portal/Field; separate Edge and Edge Class contracts; Event Handler/Method/Script; Membrane. Update the index as each spec exists, not only at the end. Existing source authority remains github://mikemartinez1974/public/primitives/root.node; use portals instead of a second editable mirror. Runtime gaps remain in tasks/declaration-surfaces and linked follow-ups, not silently declared shipped by documentation work.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Every agreed library concept has a linked spec; semantic classification is independent of node-type representation",
          "All specs contain eight sections, including Declaration Behavior, and distinguish agreed semantics, implementation evidence, gaps and open decisions",
          "View and Glyph specs explicitly permit a glyph-shaped View without requiring an icon category",
          "View, Surface and Membrane document fixed workspace geometry, explicit manual resizing, internal clipping and exposed boundary controls",
          "Automated checks verify structure, links, geometry and recorded evidence paths; focused behavior tests verify the claims they actually exercise",
          "The index is current and stale lists point to the canonical source; source identities and addresses are preserved"
        ],
