      "data": {
        "title": "5. Content",
        "body": "Durable material: `data.content = { kind, value }` with kind markdown, html, svg, canvas, text, json or image (normalization support; renderer coverage varies). A View owns Content or delegates to it through `surface-delegate`.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/ContentNode.js`, `createDefaultContentNode`, `tests/contentPayload.test.js`, `contentCreationSurfaces.test.js`, `contentNodePaper.test.js`, and the \"View and Content contract\" section of `graph-native-node-composition.md`.\n\nWatch for: the older `markdown` and `svg` node types are legacy and readable, but new graphs use `content` (AGENTS.md). The spec should say so once and not describe them.\n\nReview rule: separate semantic meaning from representation, and agreed behavior from implemented evidence and known gaps.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "Lists the six kinds and what renders each",
          "Says how a View owns or delegates Content",
          "States what the legacy markdown and svg nodes are and that new graphs do not write them"
        ],
