      "data": {
        "title": "9. Portal",
        "body": "An addressed opening into another graph's exposed Port. Consumes or follows; never creates an ordinary node when followed.\n\nContract lives in the `portal` entry of `nodeTypeRegistry.js`, `data.target { mode, ref, portId, surfaceId }`, `utils/graphNavigationAddress.js` (`resolveGraphNavigationExposure`), `workspaceCapabilities.js`, and `tests/portalLegacyAnchorValidation.test.js`, `renderedPortalType.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: the `authority: navigate` field, the `mode` values (navigate, expand, open alongside per the structural inventory), and how a portal resolves when the target has no exposed Port (the landing surface fallback).\n\nReview rule: separate semantic meaning from representation, and agreed behavior from implemented evidence and known gaps.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the target shape and the mode values that are real",
          "Explains how a portal lands (landing surface, then default View)",
          "Says what happens when the target is missing"
        ],
