      "data": {
        "title": "10. Field",
        "body": "Functional data inside a graph: `key` and `value` (with a `fieldType`). Never for a graph's own title, kind or identity: that belongs to the Declaration.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/FieldNode.js`, the `field` entry of `nodeTypeRegistry.js`, `utils/editorFieldTypes.js`, and the class-backed fields (an edge-class stroke edits colour and width through its class).\n\nWatch for: a Field is \"product-owned\" for editing (`editorResolutionPolicy.js`) unless class-backed. The spec should also state how it differs from a Declaration's editor fields, which share the word and nothing else.\n\nReview rule: separate semantic meaning from representation, and agreed behavior from implemented evidence and known gaps.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States the key, value and fieldType data",
          "Says what may not be a Field",
          "Explains class-backed fields"
        ],
