      "data": {
        "title": "12. Event Handler (and Events)",
        "body": "Emitters declare their own events; an Event Handler listens to exactly one and runs the Methods through its `action-method` socket and `invokes` relationships. There are no event-declaration or subscription nodes.\n\nContract lives in `Nodes/EventHandlerNode.js`, `utils/eventHandlerContract.js`, `eventBridge.js`, `bridgeEventSubscriptions.js`, `changeAnnouncements.js`, `graphStructureEvents.js`, and the graph events section of `AGENTS.md`. Tests: `eventHandlerContract.test.js`, `eventBridgeSmoke.test.js`, `bridgeEventModel.test.js`.\n\nWatch for: the registry still has a legacy `subscription` type; the spec should name it as legacy, not as part of the model. Event Handler and Method nodes are edit-mode only.\n\nReview rule: separate semantic meaning from representation, and agreed behavior from implemented evidence and known gaps.",
        "status": "done",
        "owner": "",
        "priority": "high",
        "estimateHours": "",
        "acceptanceCriteria": [
          "States event identity (emitter id plus event key)",
          "Says how an Event Handler subscribes and what it runs",
          "Names the legacy subscription type as legacy"
        ],
