        "title": "4. How do Method and Script relate?",
        "body": "Method and Script share execution machinery but have distinct authoring contracts: Method is invokable behavior with declared effects; Script carries executable source and loading/lifecycle configuration. Current effect enforcement covers selected host calls, not the entire declared vocabulary. Both specs document this limit.",
